        "original_id": "10476757-7798-5ade-91b8-2bdb3b85151c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John Hodge, Danny Boyle, Irvine Welsh, Alex Garland\n- Works: Trainspotting, The Beach, T2 Trainspotting, Shallow Grave, A Life Less Ordinary, The Final Curtain, Alien Love Triangle, Porno\n- Roles: screenwriter, dramatist, director, novelist\n\nFacts:\n- John Hodge, born in 1964, is a British screenwriter and dramatist.\n- John Hodge is most noted for adapting Irvine Welsh's novel Trainspotting into the screenplay for the film Trainspotting.\n- John Hodge wrote the films Shallow Grave in 1994, Trainspotting in 1996, and A Life Less Ordinary in 1997.\n- The Beach is a 2000 British-American adventure drama film directed by Danny Boyle.\n- The Beach is based on Alex Garland's 1996 novel The Beach, and John Hodge adapted the novel for the film.\n- John Hodge's film credits also include The Beach in 2000, The Final Curtain in 2002, and the short film Alien Love Triangle in 2002.\n- T2 Trainspotting was directed by Danny Boyle and written by John Hodge.\n- T2 Trainspotting is based on characters created by Irvine Welsh in his novels Trainspotting and Porno.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
